\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Placement radius of every LIBERO task, computed from the shipped initial states alone --- no policy, no simulator, no training. The last column counts tasks whose identity-bearing object a single constant serves at the tolerance we measure for this controller (\S  \ref {sec:refute}). \textbf  {LIBERO-Object pins all ten of the objects its tasks are individuated by; elsewhere two of thirty}, and $^\dagger $both of those are the fixture tasks --- a drawer and a stove --- which have $R = 0$ because they are bolted down, not because a randomisable placement was frozen. On the shared container the ordering \textbf  {reverses}: LIBERO-Object pins it in $0$ of $10$ tasks and LIBERO-Goal in $6$ of $8$, whose shared objects are fixtures. So LIBERO-Object is not the suite that pins the most --- it is the suite that pins the object its tasks are \emph  {named} by, which is the distinction this paper is about and the reason the two columns are reported separately. Artifact: \texttt  {results/admissibility.json}.}}{3}{table.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:suites}{{2}{3}{Placement radius of every LIBERO task, computed from the shipped initial states alone --- no policy, no simulator, no training. The last column counts tasks whose identity-bearing object a single constant serves at the tolerance we measure for this controller (\S \ref {sec:refute}). \textbf {LIBERO-Object pins all ten of the objects its tasks are individuated by; elsewhere two of thirty}, and $^\dagger $both of those are the fixture tasks --- a drawer and a stove --- which have $R = 0$ because they are bolted down, not because a randomisable placement was frozen. On the shared container the ordering \textbf {reverses}: LIBERO-Object pins it in $0$ of $10$ tasks and LIBERO-Goal in $6$ of $8$, whose shared objects are fixtures. So LIBERO-Object is not the suite that pins the most --- it is the suite that pins the object its tasks are \emph {named} by, which is the distinction this paper is about and the reason the two columns are reported separately. Artifact: \texttt {results/admissibility.json}}{table.caption.9}{}}
