\newlabel{fig:declared}{{2}{5}{\textbf {The region a LIBERO task declares, against the states it ships.} The shaded square is the sampling box the task's own BDDL specifies; the dots are the fifty shipped initial states. \textbf {A} LIBERO-Object task $0$: a $5 \times 5$\,cm declaration, and all fifty states at one point. \textbf {B} LIBERO-Long task $0$, same generator, the identical $5 \times 5$\,cm declaration, drawn on the same scale: the states fill it. No tolerance, controller, policy or simulator enters this comparison --- it is two shipped files. Generated by \texttt {paper/render\_fig10\_declared.py}}{figure.caption.12}{}}
