\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Mean placement entropy $H_\delta $ in bits, swept over an order of magnitude in the tolerance $\delta $. LIBERO-Object is lowest at every tolerance, so the ordering does not depend on the modelling choice --- but every suite reaches zero by $\delta = 5$\,cm, which is a statement about coarse resolution rather than about LIBERO. That degeneracy is why the paper's claim is licensed on the radius $R$ (Table~\ref {tab:suites}), which has no such parameter. Artifact: \texttt  {results/placement\_entropy.json}.}}{16}{table.caption.59}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:deltasweep}{{17}{16}{Mean placement entropy $H_\delta $ in bits, swept over an order of magnitude in the tolerance $\delta $. LIBERO-Object is lowest at every tolerance, so the ordering does not depend on the modelling choice --- but every suite reaches zero by $\delta = 5$\,cm, which is a statement about coarse resolution rather than about LIBERO. That degeneracy is why the paper's claim is licensed on the radius $R$ (Table~\ref {tab:suites}), which has no such parameter. Artifact: \texttt {results/placement\_entropy.json}}{table.caption.59}{}}
